      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The hilltop Hearst Castle, built for William Randolph Hearst in the early 1900s, now draws visitors to San Simeon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Simeon%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Captain Clark erected a wharf in 1869 for whaling, but waves too high led to its abandonment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Simeon%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1958 Hearst heirs gave 137 acres, including the castle complex, to California as a state historical monument.",
